<article class="content editorial-guide">
 <p class="eyebrow">ZAKAT GUIDE</p><h1>How to estimate Zakat, Nisab and Fitrana</h1>
 <p>Zakat calculators are useful for organising figures, but deciding whether an asset is Zakatable can depend on your circumstances and scholarly guidance. Our calculators make their assumptions visible and ask you to enter prices or a published local Fitrana rate instead of presenting unverified live values.</p>
 <nav class="guide-quick-links" aria-label="Related Zakat tools"><a href="/tools/zakat-calculator/">Zakat calculator ↗</a><a href="/tools/nisab-calculator/">Nisab thresholds ↗</a><a href="/tools/gold-zakat-calculator/">Gold Zakat ↗</a><a href="/tools/fitrana-calculator/">Fitrana ↗</a></nav>
 <h2>What is Nisab?</h2><p>Nisab is the minimum qualifying wealth threshold for Zakat. The traditional gold and silver standards use different weights and usually give different monetary values. The calculator applies 87.48 grams for gold and 612.36 grams for silver, multiplied by the current price per gram that you enter. Which benchmark to follow is a matter for qualified guidance.</p>
 <h2>How a 2.5% illustration is calculated</h2><p>For wealth that meets the relevant conditions, the calculator can show 2.5% of your entered qualifying net assets. Whether and how to deduct liabilities, how to value investments or business stock, and whether a lunar year (hawl) has passed all require care. The tool is an estimate, not an automatic ruling or tax calculation.</p>
 <h2>Cash, savings and gold</h2><p>Enter asset amounts in one currency and avoid mixing currencies without converting first. The <a href="/tools/gold-zakat-calculator/">gold calculator</a> estimates pure-gold content from weight and karat purity; gemstone weight and jewellery rules may require separate consideration. You provide the metal price, because the site does not claim to receive a live market price feed.</p>
 <h2>Fitrana is different from annual Zakat</h2><p>Zakat al-Fitr (Fitrana) is associated with the end of Ramadan and is commonly expressed as an amount per eligible person. Rates and accepted forms of payment may vary by locality and authority. Enter the currently verified rate from your chosen mosque or charity; do not assume one universal worldwide cash amount.</p>
 <h2>Reviewing the result</h2><p>Keep a record of your assumptions, check current metal prices and your community's guidance, and ask a qualified scholar or trusted charity when the treatment of an asset is unclear. UK users should also verify that the currency and rates they enter are in pounds if they expect a GBP result.</p>
